# The log line ga-supervisor-cli-watchdog keys on, pinned to the Supervisor source.
#
# Source: supervisor/plugins/base.py:221-223 in greenautarky/ha-supervisor,
# branch ga/2026.10.5-wp9-3 (= homeassistant_supervisor 2026.10.5.3):
#     _LOGGER.warning("Error on installing %s plugin, retrying in 30sec", self.slug)
# with slug "cli" for the CLI plugin. The Supervisor source is NOT vendored in
# this repo, so selftest.sh checks (a) this pin == the live script's SIGNATURE,
# (b) CHECKED_SUPERVISOR_VERSION == version.yaml homeassistant_supervisor, and
# (c) when GA_SCW_SUPERVISOR_BASE_PY points at that file, the source still
# contains the format string.
#
# NEXT SUPERVISOR BUMP: (b) goes red on purpose. Re-check the line in the new
# fork (git grep "Error on installing" -- supervisor/plugins/base.py; run the
# selftest with GA_SCW_SUPERVISOR_BASE_PY=<that file>), fix SIGNATURE here and in
# the script if it moved, then update CHECKED_* below.
SIGNATURE=Error on installing cli plugin, retrying
SOURCE_FORMAT=Error on installing %s plugin, retrying in 30sec
CHECKED_FORK_BRANCH=ga/2026.10.5-wp9-3
CHECKED_SUPERVISOR_VERSION=2026.10.5.3
